Rāma bathes at apsara lake and performs evening prayer --- Rāma enters Agastya hermitage and eats sanctified fare --- Rāma sleeps content and rises for morning rites --- Rāma bows and seeks leave to depart --- Agastya hails Rāma as purifier worshipped by gods --- Rāma boards golden Puṣpaka amid sage blessings --- Rāma reaches Ayōdhyā by midday and dismisses Puṣpaka --- Rāma sends doorkeeper to summon Lakṣmaṇa and Bharata